# Strip from releng for a privacy-first live image.
cloud-init
# conflicts with systemd-resolvconf from releng
openresolv

# --- ISO size: everything below is measured, not guessed ---------------------
#
# The 2026.08.19 image was 2.95 GiB, over GitHub's 2 GiB per-asset cap, so it
# shipped as .part-00/.part-01 that every user has to `cat` back together before
# Etcher will touch it. That is step one of the install and it loses people.
# These exclusions are what put the image back under a single file. Numbers come
# from bsdtar on the shipped ISO, not from estimates.

# linux-hardened: NOTHING ON THE LIVE ISO CAN BOOT IT. Both loader entries
# (01-archiso-linux.conf, 02-cicada-ram.conf) name vmlinuz-linux. The package
# was costing 667 MiB for a kernel with no boot entry:
#     145 MiB  package in the squashfs
#     233 MiB  initramfs-linux-hardened.img
#      17 MiB  vmlinuz-linux-hardened
#     250 MiB  a second copy of both inside the embedded efiboot.img, because
#              archiso's _make_boot_on_fat copies every vmlinuz-* and
#              initramfs-*.img into the EFI system partition image
# Installed systems still get it: it stays in install-packages.txt, and
# install-chroot.sh writes the hardened boot entry when the kernel is present.
linux-hardened

# linux-firmware is a zero-byte meta package that hard-depends on every vendor
# split, nvidia included. Excluding the meta and naming the splits we want in
# packages.cicada.x86_64 is the only way to not ship the ones we do not.
# `linux` merely optdepends on firmware, so dropping the meta breaks nothing.
linux-firmware

# linux-firmware-nvidia is 110 MiB of the 152 MiB of firmware inside EACH
# initramfs, plus 99 MiB in the squashfs, plus the efiboot duplicate: 541 MiB
# in total, for discrete NVIDIA GPUs. Cicada is Wayland/Hyprland, where the
# proprietary stack is poor and nouveau is not a daily driver either. A laptop
# with an NVIDIA dGPU still boots and runs on its integrated GPU.
# Anyone who wants it back: sudo pacman -S linux-firmware-nvidia
linux-firmware-nvidia

# Marvell is enterprise NICs and embedded parts: 78 MiB with essentially no
# laptop relevance. Same one-line recovery as above.
linux-firmware-marvell
